  "stem": "A modern grand-prix racing car of mass m is travelling on a flat track in a circular arc of radius R with a speed v. If the coefficient of static friction between the tyres and the track is $\\mu_{s}$; then the magnitude of negative lift $f_{L}$ acting downwards on the car is:",
  "options": {
    "A": "$m\\left( \\frac{v^{2}}{\\mu_{s}R} + g \\right)$",
    "B": "$m\\left( \\frac{v^{2}}{\\mu_{s}R} - g \\right)$",
    "C": "$m\\left( g - \\frac{v^{2}}{\\mu_{s}R} \\right)$",
    "D": "$- m\\left( \\frac{v^{2}}{\\mu_{s}R} + g \\right)$"
  },
  "answer": {
    "keys": [
      "B"
    ]
  },
